  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the rectangular block of identical non-zero values\n    best = None\n    best_size = 0\n    \n    for val in range(1, 10):\n        # Find all cells with this value\n        cells = set()\n        for r in range(rows):\n            for c in range(cols):\n                if grid[r][c] == val:\n                    cells.add((r, c))\n        \n        # Try all rectangular regions\n        for r1 in range(rows):\n            for c1 in range(cols):\n                if (r1, c1) not in cells:\n                    continue\n                for r2 in range(r1 + 1, rows):\n                    for c2 in range(c1 + 1, cols):\n                        size = (r2 - r1 + 1) * (c2 - c1 + 1)\n                        if size <= best_size:\n                            continue\n                        # Check if all cells in rectangle have this value\n                        ok = True\n                        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                                if grid[r][c] != val:\n                                    ok = False\n                                    break\n                            if not ok:\n                                break\n                        if ok and size > best_size:\n                            best_size = size\n                            best = (r1, c1, r2, c2, val)\n    \n    result = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    if best:\n        r1, c1, r2, c2, val = best\n        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                result[r][c] = val\n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the rectangular block of identical non-zero values\n    best = None\n    best_size = 0\n    \n    for val in range(1, 10):\n        # Find all cells with this value\n        cells = set()\n        for r in range(rows):\n            for c in range(cols):\n                if grid[r][c] == val:\n                    cells.add((r, c))\n        \n        # Try all rectangular regions\n        for r1 in range(rows):\n            for c1 in range(cols):\n                if (r1, c1) not in cells:\n                    continue\n                for r2 in range(r1 + 1, rows):\n                    for c2 in range(c1 + 1, cols):\n                        size = (r2 - r1 + 1) * (c2 - c1 + 1)\n                        if size <= best_size:\n                            continue\n                        # Check if all cells in rectangle have this value\n                        ok = True\n                        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                                if grid[r][c] != val:\n                                    ok = False\n                                    break\n                            if not ok:\n                                break\n                        if ok and size > best_size:\n                            best_size = size\n                            best = (r1, c1, r2, c2, val)\n    \n    result = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    if best:\n        r1, c1, r2, c2, val = best\n        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                result[r][c] = val\n    return result",
